  "description": "Implements a PostHog API (headless) survey inside the user's own codebase so it renders with their UI components and captures the exact events PostHog expects, then verifies the first response arrived. Use when asked to implement a survey, build a headless survey, build a custom survey UI, render a survey in my app, or wire up a survey of type `api` in a browser, server, or custom mobile UI. Covers the posthog-js event contract, server-side SDK capture, and post-implementation verification through MCP. To design or create the survey definition, use creating-surveys instead. For a survey that is implemented but not showing or not recording, use debugging-surveys.",
